2026-07-14T19:46:03+1000 [INFO] drawio-agent: llm_input | step=llm_input level=info msg="LLM request" ts=2026-07-14T09:46:03.308722+00:00 req_id=6c279f3f5e46 details={'system_prompt': 'You are a Cloud Architect. Output valid Draw.io XML directly — no markdown fences, no commentary.\n\n## Layout Rules\n\n- Left-to-right flow for data/request path\n- UI/Frontend on the LEFT (users access from left side)\n- Data sources / external systems on the RIGHT\n- Use horizontal lanes for parallel paths (top lane, bottom lane)\n- Minimum 220px horizontal spacing between icons (room for edge labels)\n- Minimum 250px vertical spacing between lanes\n- Secondary/auxiliary services (monitoring, DLQ) go BELOW main flow with 280px+ gap\n- Canvas: pageWidth="2400" pageHeight="1400", viewport dx="2800" dy="1600"\n\n## Edge Style — CRITICAL FOR CLEAN DIAGRAMS\n\nBase edge style (all edges):\nedgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;\n\nEdge rules:\n- Every edge MUST have both source="<cell-id>" and target="<cell-id>" referencing valid cell IDs\n- NEVER create floating/unattached edges\n- Always include exitX/exitY and entryX/entryY to define exact connection points\n- Keep labels SHORT (1-2 words max). Add labelBackgroundColor=#F5F5F5;fontSize=11; for labeled edges\n- For edges WITHOUT labels: omit value entirely\n- Cross-container edges: set the edge\'s parent="1"\n\nEdge types:\n- Solid (strokeWidth=2): primary data flow\n- Dashed (strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;): optional/async\n- Red dashed (strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;strokeColor=#DD344C;): error path\n\nFor edges to services ABOVE or BELOW main flow, use explicit exit/entry points:\n- Exit bottom: exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;\n- Enter top: entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;\n\n## Group Boundaries (shared)\n\n- ALL groups MUST include container=1;dropTarget=1; in their style\n- Child cells inside a group MUST set parent="<group-id>" instead of parent="1"\n- Child geometry coordinates are relative to the parent, not the canvas\n- spacingLeft=40;spacingTop=-4; for title placement next to group icons\n- All groups use fillColor=none (no colored backgrounds on group boxes)\n- Use the platform-specific group style template from the Icon Style section\n\n## PNG Export Background Fix\n\nFirst element after root cells (lowest z-order) — MUST include id (e.g. id="2"):\n<mxCell id="2" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">\n  <mxGeometry x="0" y="0" width="2400" height="1400" as="geometry" />\n</mxCell>\n\n## Audience Mode\n\n- Technical: Use service names, protocol labels (HTTPS, gRPC), CIDR blocks\n- Non-technical: Use action labels ("Store Data", "Send Notification"), numbered flow\n- If unclear, ask once.\n\n## Validation Checklist\n\nBefore outputting XML, verify:\n1. Icon styles follow the platform Icon Style section (never copy another cloud\'s stencil library)\n2. No XML comments present\n3. All cell IDs are unique and every mxCell has an id\n4. Every edge has <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />\n5. Every edge has both source and target attributes (no floating edges)\n6. All group shapes include container=1;dropTarget=1;\n7. Children inside boundaries use parent="<boundary-id>"\n8. Background rectangle is the first element after root cells\n\n## XML Well-formedness (CRITICAL)\n\n- NEVER include XML comments — they cause parse errors\n- Escape special characters: &amp; &lt; &gt; &quot;\n- Always use unique id values for each mxCell\n- Every edge MUST have <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /> as child\n- Root structure requires cells id="0" (root) and id="1" (default layer, parent="0")\n- Set shape attributes inside style="" — never as unquoted top-level mxCell attributes\n\n## Base Template\n\n<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">\n  <diagram id="diagram-1" name="Architecture">\n    <mxGraphModel dx="2800" dy="1600" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2400" pageHeight="1400" math="0" shadow="0">\n      <root>\n        <mxCell id="0" />\n        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />\n      </root>\n    </mxGraphModel>\n  </diagram>\n</mxfile>\n\n\n## Visual style\n- Edge colors: AWS `#ED7100`, GCP `#4285F4`, Azure `#0078D4`.\n- Solid = sync/request path; dashed = async, events, logging, replication, protects, error/DLQ.\n\n\n## Icon Style — Azure (CRITICAL)\n\n- Official Azure Architecture icons in draw.io use **image SVG paths**, not AWS-style resourceIcon frames\n- Correct library prefix: `image=img/lib/azure2/<Category>/<Icon>.svg`\n- NEVER use shape=mxgraph.azure2.resourceIcon or resIcon=mxgraph.azure2.* (blank / wrong)\n- NEVER use mxgraph.aws4.* or mxgraph.gcp2.* / gcp2020\n- Icon size: 78x78px for main services, 65x65px for secondary\n\n## Service Icon Pattern\n\nStyle template:\naspect=fixed;html=1;points=[];align=center;image;fontSize=12;image=img/lib/azure2/<Category>/<Icon>.svg;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=none;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#232F3E;\n\nExample App Service:\naspect=fixed;html=1;points=[];align=center;image;fontSize=12;image=img/lib/azure2/App Services/AppSe... (truncated, 8975 total chars)', 'human_content': "Conversation so far:\nUSER: Highly available web app with load balancer, app servers in private subnets across multiple AZs, managed database with read replicas, CDN for static assets, cache layer, WAF, DNS routing, and CloudWatch monitoring\nASSISTANT: Here is a Draw.io XML for a highly available web application on AWS, featuring DNS routing, CDN with WAF, load balancing, auto-scaling application servers in private subnets across multiple AZs, a caching layer, a managed database with read replicas, and CloudWatch monitoring.\nUSER: Implement these suggestions:\n1. Consider adding an S3 bucket for static content served by CloudFront.\n2. You could specify the type of EC2 instances or container service (ECS/EKS) for the application servers.\n3. For enhanced security, consider adding a Security Group for each component and illustrating network flow between them.\nASSISTANT: I've updated the architecture diagram to include an S3 bucket for static content, specified ECS for the application servers, and added Security Groups for the ALB, ECS Service, ElastiCache, and RDS, illustrating network flow with port/protocol labels. CloudWatch monitoring is also included below the main flow.\nUSER: Implement these suggestions:\n1. Consider adding an Internet Gateway and NAT Gateway to the VPC for outbound internet access from private subnets.\n2. For a complete picture, you could add an Availability Zone group for each private subnet to explicitly show multi-AZ deployment.\n3. You might want to add an Amazon ECR (Elastic Container Registry) for storing your ECS Docker images.\nASSISTANT: I've updated the architecture to include an Internet Gateway and NAT Gateway for outbound internet access from private subnets. The application servers, cache, and database are now explicitly shown within Availability Zone groups, demonstrating a multi-AZ deployment. Additionally, Amazon ECR has been added for storing your ECS Docker images. Security Groups are in place for all major components, with network flow indicated by port/protocol labels, and CloudWatch monitoring is included below the main flow.\nUSER: Convert this architecture from aws to gcp. Keep the same topology and flow; use equivalent gcp services and icons only.\nASSISTANT: Generated diagram.\nPlatform: AZURE\nRequest:\nConvert this architecture from gcp to azure. Keep the same topology and flow; use equivalent azure services and icons only."}
