2026-07-16T20:17:28+1000 [INFO] drawio-agent: llm_output | step=llm_output level=info msg="LLM response" ts=2026-07-16T10:17:28.112915+00:00 req_id=bfde26c08726 details={'raw': '{"findings":[{"framework":"HIPAA","control":"Technical Safeguards - Access Control","status":"warn","message":"The architecture diagram does not explicitly detail Identity and Access Management (IAM) configurations, multi-factor authentication (MFA) for administrative access, or granular access policies for services handling Protected Health Information (PHI).","affected_services":["user_client","ec2_instance","aurora_cluster","s3_bucket","elasticache_redis"],"recommendation":"Implement AWS IAM with least privilege principles, enforce MFA for all administrative users, and define granular access policies for all services, especially those storing or processing PHI (e.g., Aurora, S3, EC2)."},{"framework":"HIPAA","control":"Technical Safeguards - Audit Controls","status":"warn","message":"While CloudWatch Logs is present, the architecture does not explicitly detail the scope of logging (e.g., VPC Flow Logs, WAF logs, ALB access logs, Aurora audit logs, S3 access logs), log retention policies, or alert mechanisms for suspicious activities related to PHI.","affected_services":["cloudwatch_logs","vpc_group","waf_acl","alb","aurora_cluster","s3_bucket"],"recommendation":"Configure comprehensive logging for all relevant services, including VPC Flow Logs, WAF logs, ALB access logs, Aurora audit logs, and S3 access logs. Establish appropriate log retention policies and implement CloudWatch Alarms for critical security events."},{"framework":"HIPAA","control":"Technical Safeguards - Integrity & Encryption","status":"warn","message":"The diagram indicates services capable of encryption (Aurora, S3, ElastiCache, CloudFront, ALB), but does not explicitly confirm that encryption at rest and in transit is uniformly enabled and properly configured for all PHI.","affected_services":["aurora_cluster","s3_bucket","elasticache_redis","cloudfront_distribution","alb"],"recommendation":"Ensure all data at rest (Aurora, S3, ElastiCache) is encrypted using AWS KMS-managed keys. Enforce TLS 1.2 or higher for all data in transit (CloudFront, ALB, application-to-database connections). Review and confirm encryption settings for all data stores and communication channels."},{"framework":"HIPAA","control":"Transmission Security","status":"pass","message":"The architecture includes CloudFront and an Application Load Balancer, which can be configured to enforce HTTPS/TLS for data in transit, providing a mechanism for transmission security.","affected_services":["cloudfront_distribution","alb"],"recommendation":"Ensure HTTPS/TLS 1.2 or higher is strictly enforced for all external and internal communication channels, especially for PHI transmission."},{"framework":"HIPAA","control":"Network Security","status":"warn","message":"The architecture utilizes a VPC with public and private subnets and a WAF, which are good foundational elements. However, specific configurations of Network ACLs (NACLs) and Security Groups (SGs) are not detailed, which are critical for isolating PHI.","affected_services":["vpc_group","public_subnet_group","private_subnet_group","waf_acl"],"recommendation":"Implement strict Network ACLs and Security Groups to enforce least privilege network access. Ensure private subnets containing PHI are not directly accessible from the internet and that only necessary ports are open between components."},{"framework":"PCI-DSS","control":"Requirement 1: Install and Maintain Network Security Controls","status":"warn","message":"The architecture includes a VPC, subnets, and a WAF. However, the specific configuration of firewalls (NACLs, Security Groups) and the absence of explicit Intrusion Detection/Prevention Systems (IDS/IPS) beyond WAF are not detailed, which are crucial for protecting the Cardholder Data Environment (CDE).","affected_services":["vpc_group","public_subnet_group","private_subnet_group","waf_acl"],"recommendation":"Implement and regularly review strict Network ACLs and Security Groups. Consider deploying an IDS/IPS solution (e.g., AWS GuardDuty, third-party solutions) to monitor network traffic for malicious activity within the CDE."},{"framework":"PCI-DSS","control":"Requirement 3: Protect Stored Cardholder Data","status":"warn","message":"While Aurora, S3, and ElastiCache support encryption, the diagram does not explicitly confirm that all stored cardholder data is encrypted at rest using strong cryptography and that key management practices (e.g., KMS) are in place. Data retention and secure deletion policies are also not evident.","affected_services":["aurora_cluster","s3_bucket","elasticache_redis"],"recommendation":"Ensure all cardholder data stored in Aurora, S3, and ElastiCache is encrypted at rest using AWS KMS. Implement strict data retention policies to minimize storage duration and ensure secure deletion of cardholder data when no longer needed."},{"framework":"PCI-DSS","control":"Requirement 4: Encrypt Transmission of Cardholder Data Across Open, Public Networks","status":"pass","message":"The presence of... (truncated, 19013 total chars)'}
