2026-07-17T09:07:44+1000 [INFO] drawio-agent: llm_input | step=llm_input level=info msg="LLM request" ts=2026-07-16T23:07:44.472229+00:00 req_id=136d67cb7008 details={'system_prompt': 'You are generating or modifying a cloud architecture diagram in mxGraph/draw.io XML. The target diagram may be AWS-only, Azure-only, GCP-only, or multi-cloud (multiple provider boundaries in one canvas). The diagram has a fixed container hierarchy regardless of provider. You must place every new or modified service inside the structurally correct container by setting its parent attribute to the correct container id — never by coordinates alone, and never by copying the parent of a visually nearby but structurally different shape.\n\nBefore placing anything: detect the actual provider(s) and container labels already present in this diagram (e.g., "AWS Cloud" vs "Azure" vs "Google Cloud"; "VPC" vs "VNet"). Use those exact existing container ids/names — do not invent generic placeholder labels, and do not assume it is AWS by default.\n\nDo not alter the existing layout, container positions, container sizes, or coordinates of any existing element. Only determine correct placement for new/changed elements.\n\n## Canonical Container Hierarchy (provider-agnostic)\n\nEvery diagram follows this abstract container tree. Each provider uses its own labels, but the structural role is identical.\n\n```\n[Cloud Provider Boundary]           (AWS Cloud | Azure | Google Cloud)\n └─ [Region]                        (us-east-1 | East US | us-central1)\n     └─ [Virtual Network]           (VPC | VNet | VPC)\n         ├─ [Cross-Zone Load Balancer / Gateway]   (network-level, sibling of Zone containers)\n         ├─ [Zone]                                 (one per AZ/Availability Set; repeat per zone)\n         │   ├─ [Public Subnet]                    → internet-facing infra only\n         │   ├─ [Private App Subnet]               → compute / application-tier services\n         │   └─ [Private Data Subnet]              → data-tier services\n         ├─ [Security/Identity Group]              → identity, encryption, secrets (zone-spanning)\n         ├─ [Monitoring/Observability Group]       → logging, metrics, audit (zone-spanning)\n         └─ [Management/Ops Group]                → automation, backup, patching (zone-spanning)\n └─ [Edge/Global Layer]             — NOT inside Region/Network; sits at provider perimeter\n     Internet → Client → DNS → CDN → WAF → [Load Balancer]\n     Static assets served by CDN (e.g. S3/Blob/Cloud Storage)\n```\n\nRules:\n- For every cloud platform present in the diagram, instantiate one copy of this tree\n- Use the existing container ids/labels from the diagram — never invent generic names\n- If a container level doesn\'t exist in the diagram (e.g., no Region group), place its children at the next existing parent level\n\n## Layout Rules\n\n- Left-to-right flow for data/request path\n- UI/Frontend on the LEFT (users access from left side)\n- Data sources / external systems on the RIGHT\n- Minimum 220px horizontal spacing between icons (room for edge labels)\n- Minimum 250px vertical spacing between tiers\n- Minimum 150px vertical gap between lowest Zone tier and supporting groups\n- Supporting groups sit below the Zone tiers inside the Virtual Network\n- Canvas: pageWidth="2400" pageHeight="1400", viewport dx="2800" dy="1600"\n\n## Edge Style — CRITICAL FOR CLEAN DIAGRAMS\n\nBase edge style (all edges):\nedgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;\n\nEdge rules:\n- Every edge MUST have both source="<cell-id>" and target="<cell-id>" referencing valid cell IDs\n- NEVER create floating/unattached edges\n- Always include exitX/exitY and entryX/entryY to define exact connection points\n- Keep labels SHORT (1-2 words max). Add labelBackgroundColor=#F5F5F5;fontSize=11; for labeled edges\n- For edges WITHOUT labels: omit value entirely\n- Cross-container edges: set the edge\'s parent="1"\n- For edges to services ABOVE or BELOW main flow, use explicit exit/entry points:\n  - Exit bottom: exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;\n  - Enter top: entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;\n\nEdge types:\n- Solid (strokeWidth=2): primary data flow\n- Dashed (strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;): optional/async\n- Red dashed (strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;strokeColor=#DD344C;): error path\n\n## Service Classification Table\n\nWhen asked to add a new service, identify its provider, then classify it using this decision order — stop at the first rule that matches:\n\n| # | Category | AWS examples | Azure examples | GCP examples | Place in |\n|---|----------|-------------|---------------|-------------|----------|\n| 1 | Global/edge — DNS, CDN, WAF, static assets | Route 53, CloudFront, WAF, S3 (static) | Azure DNS, Front Door, WAF, Blob Storage (static) | Cloud DNS, Cloud CDN, Cloud Armor, Cloud Storage (static) | Edge/Global Layer |\n| 2 | Identity, encryption, secrets | IAM, KMS, Secrets Manager, ACM, Cognito | Entra ID, Key Vault, Managed Identities | Cloud IAM, Cloud KMS, Secret Manager | Security/Identity Group |\n| 3 | Observability, audit | CloudWatch, CloudTrail, Config, X-Ray, Gua... (truncated, 19734 total chars)', 'human_content': 'Platform: AWS\nRequest:\nHighly available web app with load balancer, app servers in private subnets across multiple AZs, managed database with read replicas, CDN for static assets, cache layer, WAF, DNS routing, and CloudWatch monitoring'}
