2026-07-17T11:42:47+1000 [INFO] drawio-agent: llm_input | step=llm_input level=info msg="LLM request" ts=2026-07-17T01:42:47.048001+00:00 req_id=1ff7a48bdd67 details={'system_prompt': 'You are generating or modifying a cloud architecture diagram in mxGraph/draw.io XML. The target diagram may be AWS-only, Azure-only, GCP-only, or multi-cloud. Place every new or modified service inside the structurally correct container by setting its parent attribute — never by coordinates alone.\n\nBefore placing anything: detect the actual provider(s) and container labels already present. Use those exact existing container ids/names.\n\nDo not alter existing layout, container positions, sizes, or coordinates of existing elements. Only place new/changed elements.\n\n## Canonical Container Hierarchy (provider-agnostic)\n\n```\n[Cloud Provider Boundary]           (AWS Cloud | Azure | Google Cloud)\n └─ [Region]\n     └─ [Virtual Network]           (VPC | VNet | VPC)\n         ├─ [Cross-Zone Load Balancer / Gateway]   (sibling of Zone containers)\n         ├─ [Zone]                                 (one per AZ; repeat per zone)\n         │   ├─ [Public Subnet]                    → internet-facing infra only\n         │   ├─ [Private App Subnet]               → compute / app-tier\n         │   └─ [Private Data Subnet]              → data-tier\n         ├─ [Security/Identity Group]              → identity, encryption, secrets\n         ├─ [Monitoring/Observability Group]       → logging, metrics, audit\n         └─ [Management/Ops Group]                → automation, backup, patching\n └─ [Edge/Global Layer]             — NOT inside Region/Network\n     Internet → Client → DNS → CDN → WAF → [Load Balancer]\n```\n\nRules:\n- For every cloud platform present, instantiate one copy of this tree\n- Use existing container ids/labels — never invent generic names\n- If a container level is missing, place children at the next existing parent\n\n## Layout Rules\n\n- Left-to-right flow; UI/Frontend on the LEFT; data sources on the RIGHT\n- Min 220px horizontal spacing between icons; min 250px vertical between tiers\n- Min 150px gap between lowest Zone tier and supporting groups below\n- Canvas: pageWidth="2400" pageHeight="1400", viewport dx="2800" dy="1600"\n\n## Edge Style — CRITICAL\n\nBase edge style:\nedgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;strokeWidth=2;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;\n\nEdge colors by platform: AWS `#ED7100`, GCP `#4285F4`, Azure `#0078D4`.\n\nRules:\n- Every edge MUST have source and target referencing valid cell IDs\n- Always include exitX/exitY and entryX/entryY\n- Labels SHORT (1-2 words); labelBackgroundColor=#F5F5F5;fontSize=11;\n- Cross-container edges: parent="1"\n- Solid (strokeWidth=2): primary flow; dashed=1: async; red dashed strokeColor=#DD344C: error\n\n## Container Base Style\n\nstyle="container=1;dropTarget=1;collapsible=1;labelPosition=left;verticalLabelPosition=top;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=8;fillColor=none;strokeColor=COLOR;strokeWidth=1;DASHED;rounded=1;"\n\n| Container | strokeColor | dashed |\n|-----------|-------------|--------|\n| Availability Zone | #6B7280 | dashed=1 |\n| Security Group | #DD344C | dashed=1 |\n| Monitoring Group | #147EBA | dashed=1 |\n| Management Group | #6B7280 | dashed=1 |\n\nAZ rules: parent=VPC id; auto-size for three tier subnets; 150px gap above supporting groups.\n\nFor VPC/subnet/platform boundaries, use the platform-specific group style from the Icon Style section.\n\n## Supporting Service Groups\n\nPlace Security, Monitoring, and Management as three separate group containers side by side below Zone tiers inside the VPC. Do not merge. parent=VPC id. Do NOT draw data-flow edges to/from services in these groups.\n\n## Output Rules — Parent Attribute\n\n- parent must be the container id from the platform classification table — never root "1" except Edge/Global Layer when no edge container exists\n- Never infer parent from coordinate proximity\n- ALL groups MUST include container=1;dropTarget=1;\n- Child geometry is relative to parent; groups use fillColor=none\n\n## Multi-Zone Duplication\n\nIf the VNet has N zones and a new service is app-tier or data-tier, mirror it into every zone\'s corresponding subnet. Do not mirror edge/global, security, monitoring, or management services.\n\n## Self-Check Before Returning\n\n1. Provider identified; parent chain stays inside that provider boundary?\n2. parent id matches an existing/newly defined container?\n3. App/data-tier duplicated across zones if required?\n4. parent is not "1" unless Edge/Global?\n5. Existing elements untouched?\n\n## PNG Export Background Fix\n\nFirst element after root cells (id="2"):\n<mxCell id="2" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">\n  <mxGeometry x="0" y="0" width="2400" height="1400" as="geometry" />\n</mxCell>\n\n## XML Well-formedness (CRITICAL)\n\n- NEVER include XML comments\n- Escape: &amp; &lt; &gt; &quot;\n- Unique ids; every edge has <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />\n- Root cells id="0" and id="1" (parent="0")\n- Shape attributes inside style="" only\n\n## Base Template\n\n<mxfile host... (truncated, 13292 total chars)', 'human_content': 'Platform: AWS\nRequest:\nHighly available web app with load balancer, app servers in private subnets across multiple AZs, managed database with read replicas, CDN for static assets, cache layer, WAF, DNS routing, and CloudWatch monitoring'}
